  "explanation": "Component metrics (recall, MRR, nDCG) are deterministic because retrieval uses cosine similarity with a fixed seed for the random warm-up. End-to-end metrics vary because the LLM qwen2.5:3b is non-deterministic: even with temperature=0 and seed=42, Ollama's sampling path has platform-specific floating-point non-determinism. The observed variance (faithfulness 0.9167 vs 0.8571, abstention_correctness 0.5714 vs 0.7143) is within the spread used to set gate thresholds (C2.1). Retrieval metrics are fully reproducible; end-to-end metrics have ~10% variance across identical runs."
